>> title: Xiao Long Bao
>> category: Dumplings & Rolls
>> tags: pork, dumpling, shanghainese, steamed, aspic
>> counters: Dim Sum Counter
>> aka: XLB, xiaolongbao, siu lung bao, 小籠包, soup dumplings, Shanghai soup dumplings
>> servings: 4
>> time: 8 hr
>> step.1: simmer the skin stock 2 hr, strain, chill 4 hr
>> step.2: knead to a stiff dough, rest 30 min
>> step.3: stir one way until sticky, fold the diced aspic through
>> step.4: roll thin-rimmed rounds, pleat, twist the top shut
>> step.5: steam 8 min, and leave them to settle

Simmer @pork skin{8%oz}(225 g; blanched and scraped clean) and @chicken wings{2} in @water{4%cups}(950 mL) with @fresh ginger{3%slices}(coin-sized), @scallions{2} and @Shaoxing wine{1%Tbs} in a #pot{} for ~simmer{2%hr}, strain it into a shallow tray, and ~chill{4%hr} until it sets to a firm jelly. This jelly is the soup — without it the dish is a pork dumpling with a famous name.

Knead @all-purpose flour{2%cups}(240 g) with @hot water{1/2%cup}(120 mL; just off the boil) and @cold water{1/4%cup}(60 mL) to a stiff, smooth dough, then ~rest{30%min} under a cloth.

Stir @ground pork{12%oz}(340 g; not lean) with @light soy sauce{1%Tbs}, @Shaoxing wine{2%tsp}, @toasted sesame oil{1%tsp}, @sugar{1%tsp}, @fresh ginger{1%Tbs}(grated), @kosher salt{1/2%tsp} and @white pepper{1/4%tsp} in one direction until it is sticky, then cut @&(~2)aspic{} into small dice and fold it through cold.

Roll @&(~2)dough{} into 24 rounds, thick in the middle and paper-thin at the rim, and close @&(~1)filling{} in each one with a ring of pleats, twisting the top shut.

Steam @&(~1)dumplings{} on @napa cabbage leaves{4}(or squares of parchment) in a #bamboo steamer{} over boiling water for ~steam{8%min}, then leave them a minute before moving them. Lifted straight off the heat, a skin tears and the soup is on the tray instead of in the spoon.
